Subject: retain executed inline equation delimiter origin
Upstream-Status: ManT-owned equation snapshot evidence

roff_eqndelim() already tracks whether EQ came from active delimiters.
Retain that resolved origin when roff_EQ() allocates the equation node.
NODE_LINE records source line position independently. The owned snapshot
transfers delimiter origin to producers resolving mathematical placement.

--- a/roff.h
+++ b/roff.h
@@ -541,6 +541,7 @@
 #define	NODE_NOPRT	 (1 << 10) /* Shall not print anything. */
 #define	NODE_ID		 (1 << 11) /* Target for deep linking. */
 #define	NODE_HREF	 (1 << 12) /* Link to another place in this page. */
+#define	NODE_EQN_INLINE	 (1 << 13) /* Originated in equation delimiters. */
 	int		  prev_font; /* Before entering this node. */
 	int		  aux;     /* Decoded node data, type-dependent. */
 	enum roff_tok	  tok;     /* Request or macro ID. */
--- a/roff.c
+++ b/roff.c
@@ -3551,6 +3551,8 @@
 	n = roff_node_alloc(r->man, ln, ppos, ROFFT_EQN, TOKEN_NONE);
 	if (ln > r->man->last->line)
 		n->flags |= NODE_LINE;
+	if (r->eqn_inline)
+		n->flags |= NODE_EQN_INLINE;
 	n->eqn = eqn_box_new();
 	roff_node_append(r->man, n);
 	r->man->next = ROFF_NEXT_SIBLING;
